, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'predictive', 'start': 3839654, 'end': 3840124, 'confidence': 0.91329, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'processing', 'start': 3840172, 'end': 3841100, 'confidence': 0.99988, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'precision', 'start': 3841260, 'end': 3841884, 'confidence': 0.95287, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'weighting', 'start': 3841932, 'end': 3842540, 'confidence': 0.52758, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'angle.', 'start': 3842620, 'end': 3843100, 'confidence': 0.98194, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'What', 'start': 3843180, 'end': 3843328, 'confidence': 0.99998, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'do', 'start': 3843334, 'end': 3843408, 'confidence': 0.99988, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'you', 'start': 3843414, 'end': 3843536, 'confidence': 0.99894, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'think', 'start': 3843558, 'end': 3843696, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'about', 'start': 3843718, 'end': 3843904, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'that?', 'start': 3843942, 'end': 3844530, 'confidence': 0.99996, 'speaker': 'A'}]}, {'confidence': 0.9360007296137333, 'end': 3940210, 'speaker': 'B', 'start': 3846340, 'text': "Well, the idea is that I think about it is that from a predictive processing and also vocational inference perspective, attention can be seen as a kind of structured learning problem. I think there's a recent paper from Chris Buckley's group that shows that there should be a reprint on Archive in which basically they showed that the attention mechanism is simply learning the precision on the weight parameters specific to a data point. So this precision is not a parameter that is in the structure of the model. So it's not a model specific parameter, but it's a fast changing parameter like the value nodes that gets updated while minimizing the vibrational free energy. And once you have minimized it and computed, then you throw it away and from the next data point you have to recompute it from scratch. So yes, I think the analogy computation wise is the attention mechanism can be seen as a kind of structured learning, but a structured learning that is data point specific and not model specific. And I think if you want to generalize a little bit and go from the attention mechanism in transformers to the attention mechanism, cognitive science, I feel they're probably too different to draw similarities. And I think the structured learning analogy and how important one connection is with respect to another one probably does the job much better.", 'words': [{'text': 'Well,', 'start': 3846340, 'end': 3846704, 'confidence': 0.99996, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'the', 'start': 3846742, 'end': 3846896, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'idea', 'start': 3846918, 'end': 3847104, 'confidence': 0.99997, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'is', 'start': 3847142, 'end': 3847344, 'confidence': 0.92481, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'that', 'start': 3847382, 'end': 3847970, 'confidence': 0.99953, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'I', 'start': 3849080, 'end': 3849396, 'confidence': 0.83, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'think', 'start': 3849418, 'end': 3849604, 'confidence': 0.99997, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'about', 'start': 3849642, 'end': 3849796, 'confidence': 0.99954, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'it', 'start': 3849818, 'end': 3850004, 'confidence': 0.99916, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'is', 'start': 3850042, 'end': 3850244, 'confidence': 0.97884, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'that', 'start': 3850282, 'end': 3850870, 'confidence': 0.99854, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'from', 'start': 3851640, 'end': 3852004, 'confidence': 0.99951, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'a', 'start': 3852042, 'end': 3852532, 'confidence': 0.96, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'predictive', 'start': 3852666, 'end': 3853216, 'confidence': 0.34643, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'processing', 'start': 3853248, 'end': 3853920, 'confidence': 0.99974, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'and', 'start': 3854000, 'end': 3854436, 'confidence': 0.8, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'also', 'start': 3854538,